==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|harn}}, of {{unk|de|unclear origin}}. Despite some claims, [[w:Max Wheeler (linguist)|Max Wheeler]] writes a connection with {{noncog|eu|gernu||urine}} (probably via an {{w|Paleo-European languages|Old European}} root, esp. a Vasconic {{der|de|qfa-sub}}) is "out of the question".<ref>{{quote-journal|en|author=Max Wheeler|title=Etymological Dictionary of Basque, by R. L. Trask, edited for web publication by Max W. Wheeler|work=academia.edu|page=203|passage=}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
